      '这是早期测试版，首次安装或启用输入法时请以系统安全提示为准。'
    ]
  },
  en: {
    title: 'Maozhan Pinyin',
    eyebrow: 'macOS / Windows / iOS Input Method',
    headline: 'Maozhan Pinyin, a local Chinese input method test build.',
    intro:
      `Maozhan Pinyin (PrivatePinyin) is a Chinese input method being tested by Station Cat. The macOS build is ${macVersion}, the Windows TSF internal test build is ${windowsVersion}, and the iOS build is now available through an external TestFlight group.`,
    primary: 'Download for macOS',
    windowsCta: 'Download Windows beta',
    iosCta: 'Join iOS TestFlight',
    secondary: 'View download info',
    downloadHref: privatePinyinProduct.downloadPagePath,
    featuresTitle: 'What this build is for',
    features: [
      ['Local Chinese typing', 'The focus is making daily pinyin input feel steady, with candidates, punctuation, and typing flow improving over time.'],
      [`macOS ${macVersion}`, 'Adds local trigram prediction so the two most recently selected words can shape the next candidate, with recent habits gradually replacing older ones.'],
      [`Windows ${windowsVersion} internal test`, 'The Windows EXE internal test build has been refreshed for users willing to help validate the TSF version.'],
      ['iOS external test', 'iPhone and iPad users can join through TestFlight to help validate the mobile keyboard, candidates, and typing flow.'],
      ['Clear download trail', 'The installer, version, size, and SHA-256 checksum are kept together on the download page.']
    ],
    notesTitle: 'Release status',
    notes: [
      `Current versions: Windows ${windowsVersion}; macOS ${macVersion}`,
      `${macDownload.platform}, ${macDownload.architecture}, ${macDownload.minimumSystem}`,
      `After installing, add "${inputSourceName}" (PrivatePinyin) in System Settings > Keyboard > Input Sources.`,
      'The macOS installer supports Apple Silicon Macs only. Intel Macs are not supported yet.',
      windowsDownload ? `${windowsDownload.platform} ${windowsDownload.architecture} internal test build is available as an EXE installer. It is unsigned and may trigger SmartScreen prompts.` : '',
